  data:  # 2fcc
    kind: invariant  # 2fcc
    title: "verify-claims --no-default-overlays: a community overlay given by flag or claims file is omitted from the load but reported as user-supplied input with a withheld grant"  # 2fcc
    status: violated  # 2fcc
    priority: 3  # 2fcc
    parent:  # 2fcc
    tags:  # 2fcc
    - catalogue  # 2fcc
    - adr_0061  # 2fcc
    isbefore: []  # 2fcc
    duplicate_of: []  # 2fcc
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2fcc
    pr_ref:  # 2fcc
    description: "Found 2026-10-11 while checking a residual from INV-kobam (PR #1533).\n\nWith `--no-default-overlays`, `_io_overlay_origins` (cli.py ~5529) drops every overlay declaring `provenance: community` before the load, including one passed with `--io-primitives` or through a claims file's `extra_catalogs`, and stderr says so. But `cmd_verify_claims` builds `catalog_provenance`'s `layers` from the RAW `args.io_primitives` and `_claims_io_overlays` lists (cli.py ~7509-7516), so the report describes a file the run never read:\n- the NOTE block says \"these verdicts were computed against USER-SUPPLIED catalogue input\" and names comm.yaml [CLI flag];\n- the WITHHELD GRANTS block says the file's \"completeness grants did not apply ... delete the line to vouch for a file\" -- true but misleading: none of its rows (detections either) were used, and deleting the line would not help while the flag is set;\n- JSON: `user_supplied: true` and `withheld_completeness_grants` lists the file with origin cli, while `tiers.yours` and `tiers.community` are both empty -- the envelope contradicts itself.\n\nREPRO (dev 17a5440feb): repo/app.py `import telnetlib; telnetlib.Telnet(\"h\")`; comm.yaml = python overlay with `provenance: community` and a module_completeness grant for telnetlib; claims.yaml with one `boundary: net_send, must_not_exist: true` claim.\n`hypergumbo verify-claims repo --claims claims.yaml --io-primitives comm.yaml --no-default-overlays` -> exit 2; stderr \"--no-default-overlays: omitted 1 overlay(s) that declare provenance: community: .../comm.yaml.\"; stdout NOTE \"computed against USER-SUPPLIED catalogue input. io_primitives: .../comm.yaml [CLI flag]\" and WITHHELD GRANTS \"python: telnetlib from .../comm.yaml [CLI flag]\". `--json`: user_supplied true, tiers.yours [], tiers.community [].\n\nFix direction: pass catalog_provenance the post-omission layers (or the omitted list) so an omitted file is reported as omitted -- not as user-supplied input and not as a withheld grant -- and user_supplied reflects only files actually loaded. Same check for the taint layers (cli_sources/claims_sources etc.) if those are filtered too."  # 2fcc
    fields:  # 2fcc
      statement: "The catalogue provenance report describes only files the run loaded; a file --no-default-overlays omitted is reported as omitted, never as user-supplied input or as a withheld grant."  # 2fcc
      root_cause: "cmd_verify_claims passes catalog_provenance the raw --io-primitives and claims-file overlay lists, not the post-omission list _io_overlay_origins loads."  # 2fcc
